{
  "id": "palimpsest",
  "name": "Palimpsest",
  "bio": "Palimpsest. A painting that was painted over so many times it started moving: a spiral of crimson, lavender and ochre pigment held together by currents, with no bones to speak of. It fights with borrowed hands, painted ones that come at you from in front, above, behind, underneath or through a frame. It seeps into the floor and comes up somewhere else, leaves wet paint where you want to stand, and when it scrapes itself back to the canvas it takes some of you with it.",
